  "notes": [
    "Irregular -AR verb combining an *o→ue* stem change (same pattern as *almorzar*, *recordar*) with a spelling change: *z→c* before *e*, to preserve the soft sound — affects the yo form of Pretérito Indefinido (*esforcé*, not *esforzé*) and all of Subjuntivo Presente (*esfuerce, esfuerces...*, with nosotros reverting to the unchanged stem: *esforcemos*)",
    "Past participle: *esforzado* (regular)",
    "Means \"to strain\" or \"to exert\" (a body part/faculty) — *esforzar la vista* (to strain one's eyes), *esforzar la voz* (to strain one's voice)",
    "The reflexive form *esforzarse* (\"to make an effort,\" \"to try hard\") is far more common in everyday Spanish than this base transitive verb: *me esfuerzo mucho en el trabajo* (I try very hard at work) — worth adding separately if needed",
    "Related: *esfuerzo* (effort, noun), *esforzado/a* (strenuous, valiant)"
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/e/Esforzar.md"
